.TH TX\-DECODE 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.2" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
tx\-decode \- one transaction on stdin (hex/base64 raw tx, PSBT, EVM RLP, or a JSON line with
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tx\-decode [\-\-chain btc|ltc|doge|eth|...] [\-\-text] [\-\-prevtxs FILE] < transaction \-> JSON lines (or plain summary)
       tx\-decode \-\-nvc\-json TXID < api.novaco.in gettransaction JSON \-> raw tx hex (fails unless the hash is TXID)
       rpc URL rawtx TXID [BLOCKHASH] | tx\-decode                      decode a tx fetched by rpc (its JSON line has "tx")
       rpc URL rawtx TXID > t; rpc URL prevtxs < t > p; tx\-decode \-\-prevtxs p < t   input amounts + fee
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
"psbt"/"tx"/"unsigned_tx"/"signed_tx") \-> public JSON lines, or \-\-text for a human summary.
Offline, no keys, never opens a network connection. Flags: \-\-chain btc|ltc|doge (address
encoding for UTXO txs; eth insists on an EVM tx, which is otherwise auto\-detected: legacy, 2930, 1559, 4844, 7702), \-\-text, \-\-nvc\-json TXID (Novacoin explorer JSON on stdin \-> raw hex,
hash\-checked against TXID), \-\-prevtxs FILE (full previous transactions, one per line as hex or a
JSON line with "tx"/"hex", e.g. the output of `rpc URL prevtxs` or `rpc URL rawtx`): input
amounts and the fee are filled in for a raw UTXO tx. A prev tx counts only if it hashes to the
input's outpoint txid; an input with no matching prev tx stays unknown (warning prevout_missing);
a prev tx matching no input is refused (prevtx_unused). Fetching prev txs is rpc's job (its
allowlist, deny\-list and credential redaction apply); tx\-decode itself stays offline.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
  \-\-prevtxs FILE: previous txs, one per line (hex, or JSON with "tx"/"hex"); each must hash to an input's outpoint
  txid (else prevtx_unused); inputs without one warn prevout_missing. tx\-decode never opens a socket.
  EVM (legacy, EIP\-2930, EIP\-1559, EIP\-4844 incl. the blob network form, EIP\-7702; signed or unsigned) is detected
  from the bytes, also in an `rpc URL eth_getRawTransactionByHash` reply; \-\-chain eth only refuses non\-EVM input (not_evm).
  Same summary keys as the UTXO path (chain, type, signed, txid, inputs, outputs, warnings) plus from, to, nonce, gas,
  value, tx_type, data, access_list, v/r/s and the per\-type fee fields; no per\-input/output lines.
  \-\-chain xlm|algo|atom|ton|ada|dot runs `acct\-tx decode \-\-chain C`, sol|tron `sol\-tron\-tx decode \-\-chain C`, xrp `xrp\-tx decode`
  (same directory, same output as calling them; \-\-testnet passed through): one decode verb for every chain.
  Input is read from stdin only; a hex argument is not read (bad_transaction on empty stdin).
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
tx\-decode: one transaction on stdin (hex/base64 raw tx, PSBT, EVM RLP, or a JSON line with
"psbt"/"tx"/"unsigned_tx"/"signed_tx") \-> public JSON lines, or \-\-text for a human summary.
